# broiler-shared-package pin 1
#
# One package of the committed, hash-pinned feed (decision SJL-D-4 (c); milestone SJL-2.7): a shared
# JavaScript library package whose home is the Broiler.JS repository, retained here byte for byte so
# that a restore needs no other repository's folder and no network for it. NuGet.config's package
# source mapping sends the Broiler.ECMAScript prefix to this directory and to nuget.org; the lock
# file of a project that references it records `content-hash`, and rule I1 holds that hash to this
# pin and to the allow-list.
#
# HOW IT WAS TAKEN. The package exactly as the Broiler.JS repository's publish-shared workflow pushed
# it to nuget.org on 2026-10-19 (run 39312237448, its artifact shared-packages, whose digest GitHub
# records as sha256:9d5dc3befeed1a361e53d65ce6af19eff1dea3cb16f9ff0aba1640e2828eaf46 and the zip as
# downloaded has), packed from `upstream-commit` and tagged ecmascript-v0.1.0-preview.7; the nuspec's
# repository element records the same commit, which rule I7 reads. nuget.org serves the same package
# with its repository signature (.signature.p7s) added: the package downloaded from nuget.org, with
# that entry taken out, is this file byte for byte. NuGet's content hash of a signed package leaves the
# signature out, so a restore from either source records `content-hash`, the base64 SHA-512 of this
# file's bytes. `sha256` is over the same bytes.
#
# (Revised 2026-10-19, when 0.1.0-preview.7 replaced 0.1.0-preview.6: decision D12 of Broiler.VM's
# JSD-0078. Between Broiler.JS fc829f8a, which published 0.1.0-preview.6, and `upstream-commit`, the
# library's code changes in NudgeToZonedTime alone, with its tests, its assurance fingerprints, its
# adapter guide, the shared changelog and the version suffix. The preview.6 pin's identity lines read:
#   content-hash PERCRai0B9fgQc9YeyREvInd0sdJUDdoiHmBoku6M8BZPzYLrXBaC+AKTpMNRtFFMs1rM8NO4vAEmTvRbzQfgQ==
#   sha256 e83be39876b9489ab101ca018e953523a51c6f58fadee95b9e8aa5bc31581f64
#   upstream-commit fc829f8a507295185527e4175e70d74e15630fd1)
#
# WHAT IT IS. The Temporal core of the shared algorithms library (milestone SJL-10.3; Broiler.VM's
# JSD-0078), namespace Broiler.ECMAScript.Temporal - the records and limits, balancing, regulation and
# addition, the ISO 8601 / RFC 9557 grammar, serialization, the formula calendars and the table
# calendars over SJL-8's years with month codes, eras and reference years, durations with rounding
# relative to a date, and the differences, with the rules of their options - beside the
# number-conversion, numerics, text, Date and time-zone and calendar areas of 0.1.0-preview.5,
# unchanged: admitted for PRODUCT use by Broiler.VM.Profile.JavaScript and
# Broiler.VM.Profile.JavaScript.Compiler since SJL-10.4, and restored by the admission probe. Its one
# change from 0.1.0-preview.6 is decision D12: where a zone's skipped day leaves the day span
# NudgeToZonedTime asserts (s7.5.35 step 8) without the duration's sign, the rounding answers
# OutOfRange, which this family maps to a RangeError, where 0.1.0-preview.6 answered a duration. It
# carries no third-party component beyond 0.1.0-preview.5's; its Temporal code is ported from this
# repository's JsTemporalCore, JsTemporalParser, JsTemporal and JsCalendars, which its
# THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md names. It carries no table: the calendar years are read from the tables
# each engine embeds (decision SJL-D-6 (c)). It is on nuget.org since 2026-10-19, as a Broiler.VM
# package release that depends on it requires (eng/verify-feed.ps1).

id Broiler.ECMAScript.Algorithms
version 0.1.0-preview.7
file Broiler.ECMAScript.Algorithms.0.1.0-preview.7.nupkg
content-hash n4IeuLVaYtO4ti3ydsLSMQMd7wcqIwyou2c7aZ4XjGBk1BwZDlX5RXztjBy4cB9t28+KKsvbL0/6wuExLF+90w==
sha256 25567501d1168da69ae43ee5bd473b554d8b37ee26b14b1ed8636ccd2b806338
upstream Broiler-Platform/broiler.js
upstream-commit 5ddee4044c0be685e07b6da326af2e22acbb912e
